@0 = ~Enable BG2-style HLAs in IWDEE (standalone Infinity UI++ support)~
@1 = ~This component is only for Icewind Dale: Enhanced Edition.~
@2 = ~Infinity UI++ must be installed first.~
@3 = ~UI.MENU is missing; Infinity UI++ must be installed correctly first.~
@4 = ~The bundled IWDEE HLA progression table is missing. Re-extract the complete IWDEE Tweaks and Fixes package and try again.~
@5 = ~SW1H01.ITM is missing from the game; the local HLA compatibility marker cannot be generated safely.~
@6 = ~WARNING: Skills and Abilities #710 and/or #720 is already installed. Recommended order is IWDEE Tweaks and Fixes component 0 first, then S&A #710/#720, while skipping S&A #730.~
@7 = ~Could not safely identify a unique Infinity UI++ rgIsIwdHlaEnabled flag in UI.MENU. Installation was stopped to avoid a partial HLA setup.~
@8 = ~Skills and Abilities component #730 is already installed. Uninstall #730 before using this component; IWDEE Tweaks and Fixes component 0 replaces its IWDEE HLA-enabling role.~
@10 = ~Resist Magic~
@11 = ~War Cry~
@12 = ~WARNING: A Ranger HLA table containing Tracking does not have the expected 10-column HLA layout. That class/kit was left on its existing HLA table and the Tracking cleanup was skipped for it.~
@13 = ~WARNING: Could not find the Ranger class/kit entry in LUABBR.2DA while applying the Tracking HLA cleanup. That class/kit was left unchanged.~

@20 = ~Expanded Triple-Class HLA Tables (Fighter/Mage/Thief and Fighter/Mage/Cleric)~
@21 = ~IWDEE HLA support is not active. Install IWDEE Tweaks and Fixes component 0 or another IWDEE HLA-enabling component first.~
@22 = ~LUABBR.2DA is missing; triple-class HLA routing cannot be patched.~
@23 = ~WARNING: Tweaks Anthology component #2090 (Remove experience cap) was not detected. Triple-class mage HLAs require a sufficiently high XP cap; install #2090 or an equivalent XP-cap removal before normal play.~
@24 = ~Could not find FIGHTER_MAGE_THIEF in LUABBR.2DA; its HLA table was not rerouted to LUFMT.2DA.~
@25 = ~Could not find FIGHTER_MAGE_CLERIC in LUABBR.2DA; its HLA table was not rerouted to LUFMC.2DA.~
@26 = ~Neither LUFMC.2DA nor its Fighter/Cleric source LUFC0.2DA is available. The Fighter/Mage/Cleric HLA table cannot be built safely.~
@27 = ~Neither LUFMT.2DA nor its Fighter/Thief source LUFT0.2DA is available. The Fighter/Mage/Thief HLA table cannot be built safely.~
@28 = ~WARNING: Skills and Abilities #710/#720 is already installed. For full integration, install this triple-class component before S&A #710/#720 and then reinstall those S&A components if necessary.~
@29 = ~LUFMC.2DA was not present; created it dynamically from the installation's current LUFC0.2DA before applying the triple-class HLA expansion.~
@37 = ~LUFMT.2DA was not present; created it dynamically from the installation's current LUFT0.2DA before applying the triple-class HLA expansion.~

@30 = ~Thief Skill Points in Multiples of Five (Infinity UI++ compatible)~
@31 = ~Infinity UI++ must be installed first for this compatibility component.~
@32 = ~UI.MENU is missing; Infinity UI++ must be installed correctly first.~
@33 = ~THIEFSKL.2DA is missing; thief skill point awards cannot be adjusted.~
@34 = ~Could not safely find Infinity UI++'s thief-skill +/- calls in UI.MENU. No UI changes were installed.~
@35 = ~THIEFSKL.2DA does not have the expected START_POINTS / LEVEL_POINTS layout.~
@36 = ~Sword Coast Stratagems component #4115 is already installed. Do not install both versions of the thief-skill x5 tweak.~

@40 = ~Remove Summoning Cap for Celestials (Planetars and Devas)~
@41 = ~SUMMLIMT.2DA is missing; the Enhanced Edition celestial summoning cap cannot be adjusted safely.~
@42 = ~Tweaks Anthology component #2340 is already installed. Do not install both versions of the celestial summoning-cap tweak.~
@43 = ~SUMMLIMT.2DA does not have the expected row/limit layout.~
@44 = ~Could not find the CELESTIAL row in SUMMLIMT.2DA; the summoning cap was not changed.~

@50 = ~Make Enhanced Bard Song Switchable~
@51 = ~SPCL920.SPL is missing; Enhanced Bard Song cannot be made switchable safely.~
@52 = ~#BARD1.SPL is missing; IWDEE's selectable Bard Song template is unavailable.~
@53 = ~Could not identify exactly one Change Bard Song effect in SPCL920.SPL. Installation was stopped to avoid creating an invalid Enhanced Bard Song selector.~
@54 = ~The Bard Song resource referenced by SPCL920.SPL is missing.~
@56 = ~#BARD7.SPL already exists. Another mod appears to provide an Enhanced Bard Song selector; do not install two implementations.~
@57 = ~Enhanced Bard Song~
@58 = ~Enhanced Bard Song: Selects Enhanced Bard Song as the active Bard Song.~

@70 = ~Bardic Wonders Extend Revised Bard Song Mechanics to IWDEE Classic Songs~
@71 = ~Bardic Wonders-style Revised Bard Song Mechanics runtime resources were not detected. Install Revised Bard Song Mechanics first before using this compatibility component.~
@72 = ~One or more of IWDEE's six classic Bard Song selectors (#BARD1-#BARD6) is missing; the classic-song conversion cannot be applied safely.~
@73 = ~Revised Bard Song Mechanics was detected, but no already-transformed Bard Song wrapper could be found to use as a structural template.~
@74 = ~A Revised Bard Song Mechanics wrapper was detected, but its song-payload marker could not be identified safely.~
@75 = ~The EFF resource used by the detected Revised Bard Song Mechanics wrapper is missing.~
@76 = ~One of IWDEE's classic Bard Song selectors does not contain exactly one Change Bard Song effect. The conversion was stopped to avoid patching the wrong song.~
@77 = ~A Bard Song resource referenced by one of IWDEE's classic selectors is missing.~
@78 = ~Revised Bard Song Mechanics was detected, but C0SINGI2 does not contain a usable song-cleanup entry to clone safely.~
@79 = ~An internal IWDEE classic Bard Song selector could not be mapped to its song index.~
